      "sequence_position": 7,
      "problem": "A diver descends a total of $32.5\\,\\text{m}$ over $5$ minutes at a constant rate. What is the change in elevation each minute?",
      "worked_solution": "Since the diver's elevation decreases by $32.5\\,\\text{m}$ over $5$ minutes, the total change is $-32.5\\,\\text{m}.$\n\nThis change occurs evenly over $5$ minutes, so we divide the total change by $5:$\n\n$$\n-32.5÷5\n$$\n\nEvaluating the quotient, we get\n\n$$\n-32.5÷5=-6.5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the change in elevation each minute is $-6.5\\,\\text{m}.$",
